{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>zarzir</b> — a name of an animal, in construct state with the word <i>motnayim</i> — meaning <i>zarzir motnayim</i> (zarzir of loins). It is mentioned because it is swift on its feet and strides well, for in time of need it can overtake its prey." "Another interpretation: bees. Another interpretation: an eagle, or a male goat that strides well in its walking, for the flock will not pass before it, and the meaning is like goats before a flock." "<b>El</b> — it is not a term of conciliation." "<b>kum</b> — a noun [passive participle], like <i>sug lav</i> (turned of heart), meaning that no man is raised up to fight against him; then he strides well, for on account of his righteousness no adversary stands against him."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:45.061761933Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}